menu "Speech recognizer engine"

choice ASR_ENGINE
    prompt "Engine that turns a TALK clip into word hypotheses"
    default ASR_ENGINE_DIY
    help
        All engines give the same output (voice_hyp_t: up to 5 guesses of lexicon word ids,
        confidences and a reject score), so the form engine (components/vform) and the router
        do not care which one runs. Bench them for speed, size and agreement.

config ASR_ENGINE_DIY
    bool "DIY int8 phoneme CTC model (pipeline/speech/fasr), plain C kernels"
    help
        Preferred. Causal depthwise-conv CTC model (0.5-1 M params), log-mel front end,
        lexicon-trie beam search with <unk> garbage, calibrated reject. Checked bit for bit against
        the speech thread's Python (host tests in this folder). Model/lexicon/calibration come from
        the cart's ASRM/LEXI/ASRC chunks (firmware/tools/cart_add.py).

config ASR_ENGINE_ESPDL
    bool "Same fasr model run through ESP-DL"
    help
        The fasr ONNX export quantized for ESP-DL. NOT BUILT YET.

config ASR_ENGINE_MULTINET
    bool "ESP-SR MultiNet (fallback, fixed phrase list)"
    help
        What main/voice.c does today: MultiNet with the phrase list in library/phrases.txt.
endchoice

config ASR_MAX_HYPS
    int "n-best guesses kept"
    range 1 5
    default 5

endmenu
